Hi all,

This is to announce that sysstat 9.0.5 has been released and is 
available for download.

With this version, sysstat can now pretty-print device names whose minor 
numbers are greater than or equal to 256. This should prove useful 
especially on large Linux clusters.

Sysstat 9.0.5 is available for download from my web page at:
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

288kB sysstat-9.0.5.tar.gz
235kB sysstat-9.0.5.tar.bz2
292kB sysstat-9.0.5-1.src.rpm
270kB sysstat-9.0.5-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat, pidstat and sa 
tools. Check out http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/features.html
to get a view of sysstat's main features.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> orange <dot> fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 9.0.4 are:
* sysstat should now be able to pretty print device names whose minor 
numbers are greater than or equal to 256. (Tests have been made on a 
large 26TB RHEL5/PP Linux cluster.)
* sadc manual page updated.
* NLS updated.
* FAQ updated.

